# Code owners for atif-sql.
#
# One owner, every path. There is no GitHub team behind this repository, so
# naming one would produce a review request that can never be satisfied — GitHub
# silently drops an unresolvable CODEOWNERS entry and the path ends up with no
# owner at all, which is worse than the obvious rule below.
#
# CODEOWNERS only REQUESTS review. It becomes a gate when the branch protection
# rule on `main` turns on "Require review from Code Owners"; without that setting
# this file is a notification list. `RELEASING.md` lists the repository settings
# the release flow depends on, including that one.
#
# Last matching pattern wins, so this single line owning everything must stay
# last if any narrower rule is ever added above it.

* @theagenticguy
